:: Statement-only formalization of the "Schroeder-Bernstein Theorem" from
:: Hundred Theorems artifact 025. Injections between two sets in both
:: directions imply a bijection between them. This file contains no proof.

environ
  vocabularies RELAT_1, FUNCT_1, FUNCT_2;
  notations XBOOLE_0, RELAT_1, FUNCT_1, FUNCT_2;
  constructors RELAT_1, FUNCT_1, FUNCT_2;
  registrations RELAT_1, FUNCT_1, FUNCT_2;

begin

::$P-
theorem
  for A,B being set,
      f being Function of A,B,
      g being Function of B,A st
    f is one-to-one & g is one-to-one
  holds ex h being Function of A,B st
    h is one-to-one & rng h = B
proof
end;
::$P+
